  "stream_step1_title": "Pick a team (Fearless tab)",
  "stream_step1_desc": "Before selecting a Pokémon, click <span class=\"highlight-purple\">🟣 Purple</span> or <span class=\"highlight-orange\">🟠 Orange</span> to assign picks to the right team. If no team is selected, the Pokémon will be added without a colored border.",
  "stream_step2_title": "Select Pokémon",
  "stream_step2_desc": "Click on Pokémon cards in the right list. They appear in the left panel with the active team's border color. Click again to remove them.",
  "stream_step3_title": "Bans tab",
  "stream_step3_desc": "In the ⛔ Bans tab, choose the ban order: Purple first (P-O-P-O-P-O), Orange first (O-P-O-P-O-P), or Free (3 Purple then 3 Orange automatically). Click Pokémon to ban them — the team color is assigned automatically. Use the '+ Empty ban' card to add a ban without showing a Pokémon.",
  "stream_step4_title": "Select the map",
  "stream_step4_desc": "Choose the match map at the bottom of the left panel: <span class=\"highlight\" style=\"color:#4caf82\">Rayquaza</span>, <span class=\"highlight\" style=\"color:#ff7043\">Groudon</span> or <span class=\"highlight\" style=\"color:#4fc3f7\">Kyogre</span>. The selected map is shown in its own dedicated <strong>Map Overlay</strong>.",
  "stream_step5_title": "Setup in OBS — 4 Browser Sources",
  "stream_step5_intro": "You need to create <strong>four Browser Sources</strong> in OBS:",
  "stream_step5_controller_label": "Controller",
  "stream_step5_controller_desc": "the main control window (keep open, but off-stream)",
  "stream_step5_picks_label": "Picks Overlay",
  "stream_step5_picks_desc": "shows each team's selected Pokémon",
  "stream_step5_bans_label": "Bans Overlay",
  "stream_step5_bans_desc": "shows all 6 bans (3 per team)",
  "stream_step5_map_label": "Map Overlay",
  "stream_step5_map_desc": "shows only the selected map, great for placing it anywhere on your OBS scene independently",
  "stream_step6_title": "Recommended dimensions",
  "stream_step6_desc": "• <strong>Controller</strong>: ~460 × 700 px (not in stream)<br>• <strong>Picks Overlay</strong>: ~750 × 220 px<br>• <strong>Bans Overlay</strong>: ~580 × 180 px<br>• <strong>Map Overlay</strong>: ~380 × 120 px",
  "stream_step7_title": "Enable transparent background in OBS",
  "stream_step7_desc": "For each Browser Source, check <strong>\"Remove background color\"</strong> (or add Custom CSS: <code>body { background-color: rgba(0,0,0,0) !important; }</code>) so the overlays blend cleanly over your stream scene.",
  "stream_tip": "<strong>💡 Tip:</strong> The <strong>📺 PICKS OBS</strong>, <strong>⛔ BANS OBS</strong> and <strong>🗺️ MAP OBS</strong> buttons open each overlay window at the right size. The <strong>✕ CLEAR</strong> button resets everything (picks, bans and map).",
